(the smokehouse).

>n

The Landing Meadow
A wide, flat meadow of soft grass where visitors, on the rare occasions that
Lamuella has any, are invited to park. The sky above it is very large and has
the look of somewhere things can arrive from. The village green is back to the
south, and a trodden path leads east towards the sound of water.

>e

The River Bank
A slow brown river that has never been in a hurry. Flat stones make a path of
sorts across the shallows, and reeds stand along the bank. Near your feet a big
flat rock sits on the mud as if it had been put there to be looked under. The
meadow is back to the west.

>look under rock
You heave the rock aside. Underneath, in the damp, lies a smooth grey whetstone,
the sort a sensible person would have kept somewhere drier.

>take whetstone
Taken.

