>sw

The Reeve's Lodge
The biggest building in the village by some margin, which is not saying much: a
round hall with a floor of beaten earth, a ring of low seats, and in the middle
a great smooth boulder that everyone calls the Hearing Stone, because that is
where the village comes to hear itself talk. The village green is back to the
northeast.

Tem, the Reeve, sits on the stone's rim with one hand to his jaw. 

>ask tem about food
"Can't chew," says Tem. "Hard crust, hard meat, hard luck. Something soft would
be a kindness: honey, that herb curd. Nothing that fights back."

>give sandwich to tem
Tem eats in small, careful bites, and his whole face loosens. "Better," he says.
"Much better. The Stone's been saying there's a ship coming. Rare for it to be
useful." He winks, which on him looks like a minor earthquake.

[The score has just gone up by five points.]

